  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933758/assets/77fe31069f53afd490d2f5b4a278e6ab0b4f14c8a69a09770e9a02abb0cebb6a.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=cos\u2061x.$\n\n- Now, compress it parallel to the $y$-axis by a compression factor of $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2}cos\u2061x.$\n\nNotice that, because the cosine function is even, it is symmetric about the $y$-axis, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}cos\u2061x=\\frac{1}{2}cos\u2061(-x).\n$$\n\nSo the graph could also be viewed as $y=\\frac{1}{2}cos\u2061(-x).$",
